Compiler for Wardscript, a typed language for trustworthy AI functions and agents

Usage: ward <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check  Type-check a program and report diagnostics
  build  Compile a program to a target language
  run    Build a program and call one of its functions
  lock   Pin the tool schemas of the MCP servers in `mcp.json` to `ward.lock`
  test   Run the program's `test` blocks against their recorded model answers
  fmt    Format files in place, keeping comments
  init   Start a project: a first program with a test and its recording
  lsp    Run the language server (LSP over stdio), for editors
  trace  Read the audit traces `ward run` and the runtime write
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
